 253:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 254:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      The compilation flag USE_HAL_I2C_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 255:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 256:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Use Functions HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() or HAL_I2C_RegisterAddrCallback()
 257:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      to register an interrupt callback.
 258:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 259:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Function HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 260:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterTxCpltCallback : callback for Master transmission end of transfer.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\sante\AppData\Local\Temp\ccxmgf1q.s 			page 6


 261:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterRxCpltCallback : callback for Master reception end of transfer.
 262:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveTxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave transmission end of transfer.
 263:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveRxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave reception end of transfer.
 264:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ListenCpltCallback   : callback for end of listen mode.
 265:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemTxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory transmission end of transfer.
 266:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemRxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory reception end of transfer.
 267:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ErrorCallback        : callback for error detection.
 268:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) AbortCpltCallback    : callback for abort completion process.
 269:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback      : callback for Msp Init.
 270:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback    : callback for Msp DeInit.
 271:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 272:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      and a pointer to the user callback function.
 273:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 274:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      For specific callback AddrCallback use dedicated register callbacks : HAL_I2C_RegisterAddrCall
 275:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 276:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Use function HAL_I2C_UnRegisterCallback to reset a callback to the default
 277:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      weak function.
 278:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      HAL_I2C_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 279:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      and the Callback ID.
 280:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 281:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterTxCpltCallback : callback for Master transmission end of transfer.
 282:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterRxCpltCallback : callback for Master reception end of transfer.
 283:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveTxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave transmission end of transfer.
 284:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveRxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave reception end of transfer.
 285:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ListenCpltCallback   : callback for end of listen mode.
 286:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemTxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory transmission end of transfer.
 287:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemRxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory reception end of transfer.
 288:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ErrorCallback        : callback for error detection.
 289:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) AbortCpltCallback    : callback for abort completion process.
 290:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback      : callback for Msp Init.
 291:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback    : callback for Msp DeInit.
 292:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 293:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      For callback AddrCallback use dedicated register callbacks : HAL_I2C_UnRegisterAddrCallback().
 294:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 295:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      By default, after the HAL_I2C_Init() and when the state is HAL_I2C_STATE_RESET
 296:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 297:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      examples HAL_I2C_MasterTxCpltCallback(), HAL_I2C_MasterRxCpltCallback().
 298:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 299:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_I2C_Init()/ HAL_I2C_DeInit() only when
 300:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 301:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_I2C_Init()/ HAL_I2C_DeInit()
 302:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state.
 303:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 304:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_I2C_STATE_READY state only.
 305:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 306:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      in HAL_I2C_STATE_READY or HAL_I2C_STATE_RESET state,
 307:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 308:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 309:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      using HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_I2C_DeInit()
 310:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****      or HAL_I2C_Init() function.
 311:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
